The answer is $\boxed{21818}$.

(Note: the statement's "220" is a lost exponent — the original problem has $2^{20}$ runners with round-$i$ payout $2^{20-i}$; with literal 220 runners the pairing rule becomes impossible after round 2. Under the true problem, $N=\prod_{i=1}^{20}C_{2^{i-1}}^{2^{20-i}}$, giving $k=\min(v_2,v_5)=\min(524287,121818)=121818$, so $k\bmod 10^5=21818$.)
